<title>PERU: Peru's October lead output falls 1.2 percent.</title>
<headline>Peru's October lead output falls 1.2 percent.</headline>
<dateline>LIMA 1996-12-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Peru's lead output fell 1.2 percent to 19,915 tonnes in October, compared with the same month last year, according to preliminary figures from the Energy and Mines Ministry released Monday.</p>
<p>Production rose 5.7 percent to 204,179 tonnes in the first ten months of the year compared with the same period last year, the ministry said.</p>
<p>In 1995, lead output dipped 0.4 percent to 232,540 tonnes compared with 233,510 tonnes the previous year.</p>
<p>Peru is the world's number three lead producer. State-owned Centromin is the country's largest producer of the metal.</p>
<p>-- Andrew Cawthorne, Lima newsroom 511 221-2134</p>
